<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;keys must be valid Perl identifiers if accessed via this module.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good point, thanks, [https://github.com/haukex/Util-H2O/commit/92de036f14|done].&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Other methods can still be called with trickery, but of course that's not really the point of this module &lt;c&gt;:-)&lt;/c&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
use Util::H2O;
my $o = h2o { '$%@.?' =&gt; 123 };
my $meth = '$%@.?';
print $o-&gt;$meth;  # prints 123
&lt;/c&gt;
</doctext>
